{
  "borough": "Camden",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those of the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application.\r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policies EN1 and EN13 [and EN31 if in a CA] of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2000.\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The facing materials to be used on the ................. shall not be otherwise than as shall have been submitted to and approved by the Council before any work on the site is commenced.",
    "Condition : 3 - Details of the coach/servicing bays and associated works to\r\n    the highway shall not be otherwise than as shall have been\r\n    submitted to and approved by the Council before any work on\r\n    site is commenced.",
    "Condition : 4 - Details of the provision for access for disabled persons\r\n    shall not be otherwise than as shall have been submitted and\r\n    approved by the Council before any work on site is\r\n    commenced.",
    "Condition : 5 - The development shall not be occupied until the whole of the car parking provision shown on the approved drawings is provided. Thereafter the whole of the car parking provision shall be retained and used for no purpose other than for the parking of vehicles of the occupiers and users of the development.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the use of the premises does not add to parking pressures in surrounding streets which would be contrary to policies RE2 [and TR17 if residential] of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2000.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - No loading or unloading of goods, including fuel, by vehicles arriving at or departing from the premises shall be carried out otherwise than within the curtilage of the building.\r\n\r\nReason: To avoid obstruction of the surrounding streets and to safeguard amenities of adjacent premises in accordance with the requirements of policy TR23 of the London Borough of Camden Unitary Development Plan 2000.  \r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - The whole of the development shall be carried out and completed in accordance with the approved drawings before any part of the building is brought into use.",
    "Condition : 8 - To ensure that the Council may be satisfied with the\r\n    external appearance of the building.",
    "Condition : 9 - To ensure that the Council may be satisfied with the\r\n    external appearance of the building.",
    "Condition : 10 - To avoid obstruction of the surrounding streets and to\r\n    safeguard amenities of adjacent premises.",
    "Condition : 11 - In order to ensure compliance with the terms of the Act and\r\n    Regulations.",
    "Condition : 12 - To ensure the permanent retention of the accommodation for\r\n    parking purposes and to ensure that the use of the building\r\n    does not add to traffic congestion.",
    "Condition : 13 - To avoid obstruction of the surrounding streets and to\r\n    safeguard amenities of adjacent premises.",
    "Condition : 14 - In order to ensure that the development is completed and\r\n    occupied as permitted."
  ],
